{
  "dom_id": "step-e6774",
  "name": "Example: Writing the Equation of a Vertical Hyperbola in Standard Form",
  "problem": "Write the equation of the hyperbola $4y^2-7x^2=84$ in standard form.",
  "worked_solution": "The Cartesian equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at the origin is\n\n$$\n\\frac{y^2}{a^2} - \\frac{x^2}{b^2}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, to write the equation of the hyperbola in standard form, we need to divide both sides of the equation by $84$ and then simplify, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{y}^{2}-7{x}^{2} & =84 \\\\ \\frac{4{y}^{2}}{84}-\\frac{7{x}^{2}}{84} & =\\frac{84}{84} \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{21}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{12} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "result": null,
